<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106150" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑᾰλο-ειδής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>like glass, glassy,
				transparent,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑγρόν</span>
			<i>vitreous</i> humour, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				14.6
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				19.358
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥλιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philol.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Placit.</u>
				2.20.12
			</span></i> (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑελ-</span></b>  ib. <i><span class="en">
				2.25.11
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ὑ. χιτὼν ὀφθαλμοῦ</span>
			the <i>crystalline</i> lens of the eye, Medici ap.<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.71
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὑ. λίθος</span> a precious stone,
			perh. <i>topaz,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Lap.</u>
				30
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑαλοειδέες . . τόπαζοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>L.</u>
					280
				</span></i>
			. [v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕαλος</span> fin.]</div>
